ers.1","W.Israel.1","Ru.Keng.Su.1","R.Balbinot.1","S.M.Morsink.1","R.C.Myers.1","Francesco.Di.Filippo.1","Warren.G.Anderson.1","F.Mellor.1","Stephen.W.Hawking.1","T.Piran.1","C.Pacilio.1","F.Saueressig.1","J.A.Pullin.1","S.Hod.1","Mohsen.Khodadi.1","Kyriakos.Destounis.1","J.T.Firouzjaee.3","D.Markovic.4","S.N.Sajadi.1","J.Mazza.1","Paul.C.W.Davies.1","M.S.Fawcett.1","P.R.Brady.1","S.Liberati.1","V.Vellucci.1","F.C.Mena.1","Matt.Visser.1","D.Nunez.1","S.Vagnozzi.1","M.H.Namjoo.1","R.Penrose.1","R.H.Price.1","J.Zahn.1","M.Sweeny.1","W.Krivan.2","Stephen.A.Fulling.1","C.Gundlach.1","Raul.Carballo.Rubio.1","K.M.Simpson.1","H.S.Reall.1","R.P.Geroch.1","A.Ori.2","P.Laguna.2","Rong.Gen.Cai.1","Davide.Pedrotti.1","A.P.Khosravi.1","O.J.C.Dias.1","A.Simpson.2","George.F.R.Ellis.1","R.Dal.Bosco.Fontana.1","P.Candelas.1","E.Poisson.1","J.B.Hartle.1","J.E.Santos.1","Edgardo.Franzin.1","S.Sinha.5","O.Luongo.1","A.Bonanno.1","T.McMaken.1","Y.Choquet.Bruhat.1","H.Quevedo.1","Reza.Pourkhodabakhshi.1","S.de.Haro.1","Alessandro.Fabbri.1","F.Eperon.1","R.M.Wald.1","F.Azhar.1","L.M.Burko.1","Ilya.L.Shapiro.1","W.G.Unruh.1"],"inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Theory-HEP","source":"arxiv"}],"first_author":{"emails":["khodadi@kntu.ac.ir"],"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/0433abe34"}],"full_name":"Khodadi, Mohsen","last_name":"Khodadi","ids":[{"schema":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7949-0441"},{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Mohsen.Khodadi.1"}],"first_name":"Mohsen","recid":1259027},"control_number":2821201,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"Elsevier B.V.","value":"10.1016/j.physletb.2024.138986"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1016/j.physletb.2024.138986"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Khodadi:2024efq"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Elsevier B.V.","value":"Unlike generic models of regular black holes (BHs) with nonzero surface gravity on both Cauchy and event horizons, an inner-degenerate counterpart with zero Cauchy horizon surface gravity was recently proposed. For this regular BH solution with spherical symmetry, we examine the stability of the Cauchy horizon from both classic and quantum mechanics viewpoints. We find that the classical perturbations do not lead to mass inflation at the Cauchy horizon, indicating classically stability, while quantum fluctuations cause it to be unstable quantum mechanically.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Elsevier B.V."}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"Unlike generic models of regular black holes (BHs) with nonzero surface gravity on both Cauchy and event horizons, an inner-degenerate counterpart with zero Cauchy horizon surface gravity was recently proposed. For this regular BH solution with spherical symmetry, we examine the stability of the Cauchy horizon from both classic and quantum mechanics viewpoints. We find that the classical perturbations do not lead to mass inflation at the Cauchy horizon, indicating classically stability, while quantum fluctuations cause it to be unstable quantum mechanically.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"Elsevier B.V.","title":"A note on the stability of the Cauchy horizon in regular black holes without mass inflation"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"A note on the stability of the Cauchy horizon in regular black holes without mass inflation"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2024-08-28"}],"curated":true},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2821201?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2821201?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2821201?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2821201?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2821201?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2821201?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3A